# Controller RF station power. libCVController.so powers the nordic link
# chip by writing the eeprom driver's temp_gpio129 attribute, but that
# node lives on i2c@89c000 which this kernel tree keeps disabled - the
# write silently fails and the station never leaves reset, so no pair
# scan can ever see a wand.
#
# The same pin is exposed by the picovr SPI driver on spi1.0 as
# picovr_gpio129. The stock vendor rc (init.picovr.rc) already powers
# the MCU and chmods this pin at on boot, so init here only re-chmods
# once the SPI device is definitely up - it must never write the pin.
# The boot loop came from init driving these nodes at a property
# trigger: a sysfs store that stalls blocks init's action queue
# (watchdog reset), and re-powering the MCU underneath its own driver
# sequence faults the bus. The station pin itself is powered by the
# shell's link layer when it attaches - the same point stock's lib
# wrote temp_gpio129, once everything has settled.

on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    chmod 0666 /sys/bus/spi/devices/spi1.0/picovr_gpio129
